        "original_id": "5607af7f-0838-5aa3-bcc0-f0fc56dc0e57",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Miklos Wright, Kevin Costner, Jeter, Bill Costner, Sharon Costner\n- Works: Open Range, Mr. Brooks, Southland, Chicago PD\n- Topics: film editing, acting roles, dedications, final on-screen appearances\n\nFacts:\n- Miklos Wright is an American film editor.\n- Miklos Wright's notable editing works include Open Range and Mr. Brooks, and both films starred Kevin Costner.\n- Miklos Wright also worked on multiple episodes of Southland and Chicago PD.\n- Open Range was Jeter's final on-screen appearance because Jeter died before the film was released.\n- Open Range was dedicated to the memory of Jeter and to the memory of Kevin Costner's parents, Bill and Sharon.",
